# Fleet choices about the mission itself, and the approach mystery thread.
# Arc and plants: content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.

card dec_halfway
type decision
cat mission
days 19 23
weight 14
once
duration 1
roles A B
lean warm feast quiet
text Halfway, by the flight plan's clock. {A} wants to break out the good rations and mark it properly. {B} would rather nobody counted yet.
option feast | Mark it | The fleet eats the good rations on seven screens at once. {A} gives a toast about the halfway mark, and it turns into a toast about the people who packed the food.
  res food -2
  morale A 4
  morale B 2
option quiet | Let it pass | Halfway passes without a word on the fleet channel. On every ship, at the same minute, someone looks at the clock regardless.
  bond A B 3

card dec_name
type decision
cat mission
days 26 34
weight 10
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious after home
text The imaging pass has turned up an unnamed crater beside the landing zone, small enough that the fleet gets to suggest a name. {A} wants to name it after the first person who ever wrote a Mars mission plan. {B} wants to name it after somewhere at home.
option after | Honor the planners | The name goes in the request. Somewhere, a committee will argue about it for years, which {A} considers part of the honor.
  set name_plan
  trait A curious 2
option home | Name it for home | The crater gets the name of a small town on Earth that nobody outside it has heard of. Within a day, the town's newspaper has a front page about it.
  set name_home
  trait B warm 3
  morale B 4

card dec_science
type decision
cat mission
days 14 24
weight 8
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious record save
text A gamma-ray burst goes off somewhere past the galaxy. Timed against the detectors near Earth, the fleet's sighting could pin the source better than ever before, but only if the ships hold attitude through the next window, and that costs propellant. {A} wants the data. {B} wants the propellant.
option record | Hold for the data | Seven ships hold still for twenty minutes. Timed against Earth's detectors, a minute or two of light away, the burst's source shrinks from a smear of sky to a point. {A} reads the confirmation and lets out a breath nobody else hears.
  res fuel -2
  trait A curious 3
  morale A 3
option save | Keep the propellant | The fleet passes. Ground telescopes get the burst anyway, less sharply. {B} logs the propellant saved, and doesn't pretend it was an easy trade.
  trait B brave 2

# --- The mystery chain (fixed days; one beat a day from 35 to 41) ------------------
card m_ripple
type event
cat mystery
clue
days 16 21
weight 14
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} cleans up the receiver's noise floor for the weekly report and finds a faint ripple in it, at about nine hundredths of a hertz. A ground loop from the coolant pump, most likely: it's on the same bus. {A} notes it in the margin and moves on to the propellant tables.
do trait A curious 1

card m_dropout
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 20 23
roles A
when since t_carrier >= 5
text {A} plots a week of the old-channel carrier for the anomaly file. It isn't steady: there most of a day, gone for a few hours, and back thirty-seven minutes later every morning. {A} blames the receiver's scan schedule, re-plots it, and the thirty-seven minutes stay.
do mark t_dropout

card m_theory
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 22 24
roles A
when since t_dropout >= 2
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
when !is A ow_letter
when !is A ow_dose
when !is A ow_hail
text {A} finds the grey relay from the manifest in the catalog: its stuck thruster left it spinning, one turn every 10.96 seconds, one orbit for every turn of Mars against the stars. Its beam, nine degrees wide, is 2.4 percent of a circle. A lighthouse nobody keeps. {A} draws it in blue marker.
do who ow_theory A
do mark t_theory
do morale A 3

card m_theory_confirm
type event
cat mystery
clue
due
once
days 25 27
roles A
when since t_theory >= 3
when is A ow_theory
text Mission Control runs the grey relay's last orbit forward for {A}: it comes round thirty-seven minutes later each morning and hides behind Mars for a few hours at a time. The ground team sends a drawing of a lighthouse. {A} tapes it beside the blue marker and sleeps through the night.
do morale A 2

card m_flash1
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 30 31
roles A
when !is A ow_theory
text {A} pulls the orbiters' night frames of the landing region, the way people look at a house before moving in. On dark ground near the edge of one frame, one pixel is lit. On the next frame it isn't. A cosmic-ray hit on the sensor, almost certainly. {A} writes down both timestamps regardless.
do set flash_seen
do mark t_flash
do who flash_who A
do trait A curious 2

card m_flash2
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 32 33
roles A
when flag flash_seen
when since t_flash >= 2
when is A flash_who
text {A} goes through every night frame of that patch from this month. Every pass, on different rows of the sensor, the lit pixel lands on the same spot of ground. Cosmic rays don't return to one address, and a hot pixel would follow the camera, not Mars. {A} sends the list round. The channel goes quiet.
do set flash_twice
do open dec_flash

card dec_flash
type decision
cat mystery
days 32 33
weight 1
once
duration 1
roles A B
when flag flash_twice
lean curious look leave
text {A} wants to ask the ground to task an orbiter for a fast sequence over the lit pixel, at the cost of a day of the fleet's downlink: every letter from home waits. {B} would leave it for the people who'll be down there with time to look.
option look | Ask for the sequence | The request goes up. {A} writes the apology to six inboxes personally, and means each one.
  set flash_looked
  morale A -2
  morale B -2
option leave | Leave it for the ground | The pixel goes into the anomaly log, under a heading {B} writes and then underlines. The letters from home arrive on time, all of them.
  set flash_left
  morale B 2

card m_key
type event
cat mystery
clue core key
due
once
days 34 34
roles A
when !fired h_dark
text In the overnight antenna log {A} finds a link request from the direction of Mars, signed with a program key the fleet still trusts, refused only because the dish was busy with Earth. Its sequence number matches one from years ago. Mission Control calls it a replay: "Not ours. Checked."
do trait A curious 2

card flash_answer
type event
cat mystery
clue core ground
due
once
days 35 36
roles A
when flag flash_looked
when since t_flash >= 5
when is A flash_who
text The fast sequence comes down overnight: forty frames of dark ground as the orbiter slides over. The pixel lights, goes out, lights again, and never moves against the rocks. Whatever it is, it isn't in orbit. {A} counts the frames between flashes, gets the same number each time, and calls the fleet.
do set flash_ground
do trait A curious 4

card flash_answer_ground
type event
cat mystery
clue core ground
due
once
days 35 36
roles A
when flag flash_left
when since t_flash >= 5
when is A flash_who
text An email reaches {A} from someone on the orbiter team who tasked the fast sequence on a lunch break: forty frames of dark ground, the pixel lighting, going out, lighting again, never moving against the rocks. Whatever it is, it isn't in orbit. The email ends: "You didn't hear this from me."
do set flash_ground
do trait A curious 3

card m_overlay
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 36 37
roles A
when flag flash_ground
when is A ow_hail
text {A} takes the old-channel receiver log, slides it back by the light time from Mars, seventeen seconds and change, and lays it over the fast sequence. The carrier peaks on the exact frame the pixel lights. Every time. It isn't two things. {A} prints both traces and pins them up side by side.
do trait A curious 3

card m_checked
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 37 38
roles A
when fired m_overlay
when flag flash_looked
text Mission Control answers the overlay in one line: nothing on their list within a hundred kilometres of that pixel still has power. They point the next backup-site survey straight at it anyway, because the fleet paid a day of letters for those coordinates. {A} reads the line twice.
do morale A 1

card m_checked_g
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 37 38
roles A
when fired m_overlay
when flag flash_left
text Mission Control answers the overlay in one line: nothing on their list within a hundred kilometres of that pixel still has power. Then, a minute later, a second line from the lunch-break stranger: the pixel is on tomorrow's backup-site survey. {A} reads both lines twice.
do morale A 1

card m_listen
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 38 38
roles A
when fired m_overlay
when !is A ow_theory
text With Mars a day and a half out, the old-channel carrier is loud enough to hear without folding. {A} pipes it into the cabin speaker for a minute: a click, a hiss, a long pause, a click. {A} turns it off before it starts to sound like anything.
do morale A -1

card m_count
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 39 39
roles A
when !is A ow_theory
text {A} times the old-channel carrier on the galley clock, the way you count between lightning and thunder. Everything about the fleet's distance from Mars has changed since the first night. The gap hasn't. {A} stops counting before the number means anything.

# --- The payoff: fires on day 40 in every season ------------------------------------
card m_reveal
type event
cat mystery
reveal
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when is A ow_theory
text The backup-site survey comes in sharp. Thirty kilometres past the zone, behind a crater rim, a ship stands on its legs, tilted, one solar wing half unfolded, its dish aimed at empty sky: Cargo 2. In the night video its lights blink, then blink again. {A} counts the gap without meaning to and gets to eleven humming the galley chime. The streak was its shadow.
do trait A curious 3

card m_reveal_any
type event
cat mystery
reveal
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when !fired m_reveal
text The backup-site survey comes in sharp. Thirty kilometres past the zone, behind a crater rim, a ship stands on its legs, tilted, one solar wing half unfolded, its dish aimed at empty sky: Cargo 2. In the night video its lights blink, then blink again. {A} counts the gap without meaning to and gets to eleven humming the galley chime. The streak was its shadow.
do trait A curious 3

card a_report
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when fired m_reveal
when is A flash_who
text {A} pulls up the report that wrote Cargo 2 off. It runs to a page and a half. The one {A} starts tonight is at forty pages by midnight, and nobody on seven ships has gone to bed.

card a_report_any
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when !fired a_report
when !is A ow_theory
text {A} pulls up the report that wrote Cargo 2 off. It runs to a page and a half. The one {A} starts tonight is at forty pages by midnight, and nobody on seven ships has gone to bed.

# --- Day 41: the window, one card per carrier branch --------------------------------
card a_window_hail
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when is A ow_hail
text 04:10. The fleet crosses inside five light-seconds of Mars, the first thing in four years close enough to answer Cargo 2 before its interlock gives up and starts again. Earth's answers always took minutes; it only ever waited eleven seconds. {A}'s standing hail goes out on schedule, the same plain words as every pass, and this time it arrives while something is listening. The light stops blinking.
do set c2_answered
do morale A 8

card a_window_quiet
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
text 04:10. The fleet crosses inside five light-seconds of Mars, the first thing in four years close enough to answer Cargo 2 before its interlock gives up and starts again. Earth's answers always took minutes; it only ever waited eleven seconds. No hail is on the schedule. {A} looks at the old channel for a long time, then at the entry checklist. Tomorrow, then. In person.
do morale A -2

# --- Day 41: the descent brief, one per arrival branch ----------------------------
card a_descent_hold
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_hold
when !is A ow_hail
text Entry is tomorrow, straight in from the crossing. The storm fills the landing zone from rim to rim, and the entry plan has a line nobody has had to write before: "if the cameras go blind, trust the radar for height and the light for place". {A} reads it to the empty cabin, to hear how it sounds.
do morale A 2

card a_descent_wait
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_wait
when !is A ow_hail
text Tomorrow the fleet skims the top of the atmosphere instead of landing through it, into the long orbit, to wait. Below, the storm lies over the landing zone like a hand over a mouth. {A} finds the light on the night frames, faint and on time, and sits down with the ration tables.
do morale A -2

card a_descent_clear
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when !flag arrive_hold
when !flag arrive_wait
when !is A ow_hail
text Entry is tomorrow, straight in from the crossing, into clear air. The landing zone is exactly where the maps said, with one more thing beside it than the maps said. {A} packs a bag for a walk: water, a torch, a roll of tape, a marker. Old habits.
do morale A 3
